==Evolution==
Evolves into '''The Majestic Zeus''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Almighty Zeus''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Zeus is basically a stronger [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], with a faster attack cycle, higher health and more range. Most notably, he has resistance to Angel enemies, which does make him a lot more effective against [[Sunfish Jones]], [[Cruel Angel Clionel|Clionel]], [[St. Dober|St.Dober]] and few other threatening ones. His very high range of 480 does allow him to counter early game anti-Bahamut threats like [[THE SLOTH]] and [[Master A.]] (450/451) but also hinders his tanking performance, as his cooldown is very long and he can't deal enough damage to get rid of threats that are already hitting him, on top of being unable to protect units with lower range.

==='''True Form'''===
Almighty Zeus only gains a small boost in stats. Although it's a clear improvement, this form is only available late in the game, where it is already not enough, as many other units you may have access to at this point, including [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]], already offer a more damaging option that also tends to last longer due to knockbacks. It is not recommended to give much priority to this form, but, luckily, it is very cheap, so unlocking it is still recommended.

==='''Talents'''===
As with many units, the standard stat boosts, '''Resist Wave''' and '''Resist Weaken''' are often situational, since few angels ([[Bears Be Back]]/[[Great Angel Chibinel|Chibinel]]/[[Winged Pigge]]/[[Mr. Angel]]/[[Archangel Exiel|Exiel]]) actually have this ability, and they don't mesh well with Zeus for their huge cost, even if you're desperate for alternatives. '''Target Zombie''' is likewise useless unless you can invest into Ultra Talents, since while he can tank, he doesn't have Zombie Killer to finish them off. Granted, your other units can achieve it, but often they are so much better at the job whereas Zeus could simply deny them the opportunity.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Zeus' Ultra Talents are the main thing giving him his relevance, specifically '''[[Behemoth Slayer]].''' It doesn't do that much for his niche of tanking, although he can get some extra defense against [[Formicidaean Ariant|Ariant]] and especially [[Angelic Beast Rajakong|Rajakong]], a fast and aggressive pusher. Where this ability shines is in his generalist value. He already has above average DPS and range, especially at level 60, where he has 13.6k. However, against [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]], he has 34.1k DPS, which is incredibly high. Zeus' matchups are also very good, only suffering against a select few Behemoths that can pierce and reach him from behind like [[Crustaceous Scissorex|Scissorex]] or [[Pterowl Hazuku|Hazuku]]. Even then, his overall bulk can give him a sporting chance against any Behemoth, similarly to [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs]]. The two combined can make these otherwise untamable enemies much more manageable. The addition of '''[[Zombie Killer]]''' with Ultra Talents supplements this boost as well, allowing him to keep Ariant and [[Lophiiformes Angaburu|Angaburu]] dead.

'''[[Shortened Cooldown]]''' puts his initial cooldown at only 79 seconds, making him easier to stack or replace. Keep in mind that the third Zeus will have his old cooldown, but often times a stage will not last long enough for this to matter. While previously his '''Slow''' Talent was inadvisable due to its pitifully low duration, it has since been directly buffed to 2 seconds duration. This gives him an uptime of 40%, which is more respectable and pairs well with his improved stackability.

'''[[Explosion Immunity|Immune to Explosions]]''' currently has limited usage since [[Explosion]] is not a very common ability on enemies. Within his targets, only [[Ange Lackey]] possesses Explosions, but he can be effective against other [[:Category:Explosion Enemies|Explosion enemies]] such as [[Xenobeast Bunaglios|Bunaglios]], [[Le'Prude]], and [[Poultrio]].

In spite of all of this, sheer NP investment required for these upgrades is simply never worth it for the typical player. The lot of these Ultra Talents are such minor improvements that only work in context with everything else, which means you can’t skip out on half of these without sacrificing one crucial aspect of his performance. At the end of it all, you’re left with only a half-decent backline tanker.

